From: Rainshower258 <188022223+Rainshower258@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 19:24:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(daemon): refuse coordinate clicks/drags outside the
 target app's windows

Coordinates are posted as real CGEvents anywhere on screen. In a bench run a
model passed screenshot pixel coordinates (2x, window-relative) as points and
clicked the user's desktop. Coordinate click/drag now fails with an error that
names the window bounds and the point-vs-pixel mix-up; element_index clicks
are unchanged.
